\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Finite energies that agree under refinement}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{The gasket graphs carry edge weights
#{\bigl(\frac{5}{3}\bigr)^n}. \ref{fdip-00DT} says that the
energy at a later level, read on an earlier vertex set,
equals the energy already present there. The same pattern
makes sense for any nested sequence of connected networks
whose energies reproduce one another exactly. The question
is which space those energies complete, and which properties
of a resistance follow from the reproduction alone.}
